{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0045","billNumberShort":"S.B. 45","billNumberLong":"SB0045S04","fileNumber":"2026FL1099","shortTitle":"Kratom Adjustments","currentSubVersion":"4","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"MCKELMK","primeSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"HALLK","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Hall, Katy","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to kratom.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>requires a kratom processor and kratom retailer to register with the Department of Agriculture and Food;<hr><ltbullet>only allows a retail tobacco specialty business to sell kratom;<hr><ltbullet>bans the sale of certain kratom products;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to penalties and fees;<hr><ltbullet>amends the age for who can purchase a kratom product;<hr><ltbullet>schedules 7-hydroxymitragynine, including synthetics, if the 7-hydroxymitragynine concentration exceeds a certain percentage as a schedule I controlled substance; and<hr><ltbullet>schedules Mitragynine pseudoindoxyl, including synthetics; and<hr><ltbullet>includes a coordination clause with H.B. 387, Kratom Modifications, directing the Legislature to not enroll H.B. 387.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Christopher Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Nate Osborne","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"LIHYRLLOCL","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-22 16:07:22.223","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-22 16:07:22.240","actionCla